# ZYREX backend — Python WebSocket service. The model (Groq via Agno) and
# the custom market-data tools (CoinAPI, GeckoTerminal, risk checks) run
# server-side with tool_choice="auto".
#   Chat:   wss://zyrex-mpya.onrender.com
#   Health: https://zyrex-mpya.onrender.com/health
# These endpoints are fixed in src/lib/zyrexApi.ts. There is intentionally
# NO model-provider (e.g. Groq) API key or endpoint in the frontend — the
# browser only ever talks to the ZYREX backend above. The browser sends
# the page Origin automatically on the WebSocket handshake; the backend
# must allowlist the deployed frontend origin (e.g. https://zyrex.wasmer.app).
#
# Max silence (ms) tolerated while connecting/streaming before giving up.
# Allow time for a Render cold start before the first token arrives.
VITE_AI_TIMEOUT_MS=120000

# Future persistence (not required for this frontend phase)
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
